git log --oneline
git diff
git stash
git restore <file>
```

### The 5 commands you'll probably use the most

```bash
git status
git add .
git commit -m "message"
git pull
git push
```

---

# 20. Important Git Concepts

```text
Working Directory
       ↓
    git add
       ↓
Staging Area
       ↓
  git commit
       ↓
Local Repository
       ↓
   git push
       ↓
     GitHub
```

And the reverse:

```text
GitHub
  ↓
git pull
  ↓
Local Repository
  ↓
Working Directory
```

---

# 21. Developer Career Rule

Don't use Git only as:

```bash
git add .
git commit -m "update"
git push
```

Use Git to demonstrate your development workflow:

```text
Issue
 ↓
Feature Branch
 ↓
Development
 ↓
Commit
 ↓
Push
 ↓
Pull Request
 ↓
Code Review
 ↓
Merge
 ↓
Release
```

This is much closer to how Git is used in professional development teams.
